WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.209
A backup is a separate recoverable copy, not merely another shortcut to the same file.

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:11.589
Recovery plans must consider accidental deletion, corruption and loss of the original device.

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:16.970
Version history helps recover earlier states, while synchronisation alone can propagate a deletion.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.762
Sync replicated the deletion.

00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:24.691
Recovery depends on separate version history, recycle-bin retention or a backup.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:29.620
Test restoration before relying on a service for important teaching material.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.047
Which is the strongest evidence that a backup is usable?

00:00:34.047 --> 00:00:38.160
A restoration check verifies that the saved data can actually be recovered.
